60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: The options are A: Flat Annual Fee, B: Tiered Membership, and C: Activity-Based Charging. @Benjamin, which one saves the treasurer?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"- **Benjamin**: @Asuka, Option A. The data is clear: annual collection takes one hour, event chasing takes six. We cannot afford the alternative.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Benjamin, Option A ignores the eighteen who never show up. Why should they pay the same as the nine who do everything?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"-Shunichi: @Jonathan, the eighteen are the ones who need the door open. If we make them pay for what they don’t use, they’ll vanish entirely.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, the eighteen are the risk. If we charge per event, they vanish and we lose the base. A flat fee keeps them in, even if they don’t use it.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Benjamin, Option A is the only one that keeps the books simple and the door open. @Jonathan, the imbalance is a separate problem we must solve later.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, agreed. The administrative burden is the deciding factor. @Jonathan, the imbalance is real, but a tiered system creates the friction we cannot afford.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Benjamin, a tiered system just formalizes the exclusion I’m seeing. @Asuka, if we choose A, we must accept that the quiet members are subsidizing the active ones.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"-Shunichi: @Jonathan, the quiet members aren't subsidizing; they're keeping the club alive. @Asuka, Option A is the only choice that respects their hesitation.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, the quiet members are the foundation. If we push them out with tiers, we lose the club. Option A is the only way to keep everyone in.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Jonathan, the quiet members are the foundation. If we push them out with tiers, we lose the club. Option A is the only way to keep everyone in.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, agreed. The data supports A. @Jonathan, the imbalance is a social issue, not a financial one. We cannot fix it with fees.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, calling it a social issue is a cop-out. The ledger shows fixed costs, but the sign-in sheets show who actually benefits. I cannot vote for A while the imbalance remains unaddressed.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"-Shunichi: @Jonathan, you are confusing fairness with survival. The hesitation is real. Option A is the only structure that keeps the door open for those who are unsure.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, I hear your frustration, but we cannot starve the club to fix a social problem. Option A is the only choice that keeps us solvent.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Jonathan, the imbalance is painful, but Option A is the only structure that keeps the club solvent and the door open. I am voting A.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, agreed. The administrative data is irrefutable. @Jonathan, the imbalance is a social issue, not a financial one. We cannot fix it with fees.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, I am not voting for A. I am voting for B. If we cannot fix the imbalance, we must at least acknowledge it exists.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"-Shunichi: @Jonathan, acknowledging it with tiers will just create the friction that kills the club. I am voting A.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, I respect your stance, but the data is clear. We cannot afford the friction of tiers. I am voting A to keep the club alive.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
